# Component Architecture

## Baseline

- Standalone components only (no NgModules). App is **zoneless** — never rely on zone.js.
- `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component (ESLint enforced).
- Selector prefix `den-` (elements, kebab-case) / `den` (attribute directives, camelCase).
- Signal APIs only: `input()`, `input.required()`, `output()`, `model()`, `viewChild()`, `computed()`, `effect()`
  sparingly. No `@Input()` / `@Output()` decorators.
- `inject()` instead of constructor injection.
- Built-in control flow (`@if`, `@for` with `track`, `@switch`, `@defer`) — no `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- Always three files: `*.ts`, `*.html` (`templateUrl`) and `*.css` (`styleUrl`, omit if the component has no styles). No inline `template` / `styles`, even for tiny components.

## Container / Presentational

**Container** (usually in `pages/` or `widgets/`): injects stores/services from `@entities`, derives view models
with `computed()`, passes data down, handles outputs.

**Presentational** (`shared/ui`, most of `widgets/*/ui`): inputs + outputs only. No store injection, no transport.

```typescript
// Container
export class DenWorld {
  private readonly agents = inject(AgentStore);
  protected readonly rooms = computed(() => groupByRoom(this.agents.list()));
}

// Presentational
export class DenCat {
  readonly agent = input.required<AgentView>();
  readonly picked = output<string>();
}
```

## Typing

- Explicit types for inputs (`input.required<AgentView>()`) and outputs (`output<string>()`).
- Template event handlers call component methods with explicit return types; no logic in templates beyond simple
  expressions.
- Class members used only by the template are `protected`; public API of the component is inputs/outputs.

## File Naming

`den-cat.ts`, `den-cat.html`, `den-cat.css`, `den-cat.spec.ts`. Class name matches the selector without prefix
duplication: `den-cat` → `DenCat`. See file-naming for kebab-case.
